ext":"\n[76] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk sed -n '22,68p' docs/projects/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":6000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[77] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\", \"AC-004\", \"AC-005\", \"AC-007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Propagate authority errors through release boundaries\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release.rs\", \"crates/callisto-cli/src/workspace.rs\"],\n        \"test\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs\", \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/durable_release_e2e_tests.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Inventory Workspace::load, version planning, release-decision derivation, build_release_intent, intent revalidation, and CLI workspace construction; preserve the M-001 locator Result through each path without fallback, logging-and-continuing, or partial lists.\",\n        \"Replace malformed-to-absent assertions with failure assertions for all four ecosystems. Add an end-to-end release-plan fixture where an otherwise discoverable package is below malformed root authority and prove no decision, intent, manifest write, Git mutation, credential read, or provider invocation is constructed.\",\n        \"Add a sibling-gap architecture test that inventories membership-reader and immediate locator call sites and rejects a bool, Option, empty glob, or best-effort parser capable of encoding invalid authority as absence.\",\n        \"Run `just test`; this batch passes only if graph and CLI release-boundary tests prove LocateError stops all release paths before decisions or operations.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): propagate authority errors to release boundaries\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"M-001\"],\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-002\", \"AC-003\", \"AC-004\", \"AC-005\", \"AC-007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Migrate all authority consumers and prove release-boundary failure\",\n      \"files\": \u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"95\" /\u003ecallisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs\", \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/durable_release_e2e_tests.rs\"]\n      },\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Inventory every read_*_membership and locator consumer with `rg`; migrate every call site to propagate Result without fallback, logging-and-continuing, or partial lists.\",\n        \"Prove Workspace::load, version planning, release decision derivation, build_release_intent, and intent revalidation all stop on authority errors before decisions or operations are constructed.\",\n        \"Replace malformed-to-absent assertions with error assertions for all four ecosystems and add an end-to-end release-plan case where an otherwise discoverable package sits beneath a malformed root authority.\",\n        \"Add a sibling-gap architecture test that inventories all membership reader call sites and forbids an unhandled or optional error result.\",\n        \"Run `just ci`; expect formatting, lint, unit, integration, release-boundary, and sibling-gap tests to pass.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): enforce workspace authority at release boundaries\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"M-002\"],\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-003\", \"AC-005\", \"AC-006\", \"AC-007\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\"batch_id\": \"M-B1\", \"title\": \"Typed Cargo and uv authority\", \"target_crate\": \"callisto-graph\", \"task_ids\": [\"M-001\"]},\n    {\"batch_id\": \"M-B2\", \"title\": \"Strict npm and pnpm authority\", \"target_crate\": \"callisto-graph\", \"task_ids\": [\"M-002\"]},\n    {\"batch_id\": \"M-B3\", \"title\": \"Authority consumer migration\", \"target_crate\": \"callisto-graph and callisto-cli\", \"task_ids\": [\"M-003\"]}\n  ],\n  \"linked_spec\": \"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \"docs/specs/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.json\",\n  \"plan_file_path\": \"docs/projects/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:231673ff3cf4c82183670dfd878b04e5e67bd3d89e4aa5e420bcbbd048d10854\",\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[78] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Run `just test`; this batch passes only if graph and CLI release-boundary tests prove LocateError stops all release paths before decisions or operations.\\\"\\n+        \\\"Run `just test`; this batch passes only if graph and CLI release-boundary tests prove LocateError stops all release paths before decisions or operations.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Run `just ci`; expect formatting, lint, unit, integration, release-boundary, and sibling-gap tests to pass.\\\"\\n@@\\n-      \\\"covers_criteria\\\": [\\\"AC-002\\\", \\\"AC-003\\\", \\\"AC-004\\\", \\\"AC-005\\\", \\\"AC-007\\\"]\\n-    },\\n-    {\\n-      \\\"id\\\": \\\"M-003\\\",\\n-      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Migrate all authority consumers and prove release-boundary failure\\\",\\n-      \\\"files\\\": {\\n-        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/workspace.rs\\\"],\\n-        \\\"test\\\": [\\\"crates/callisto-g