gration\\\", \\\"target_crate\\\": \\\"callisto-graph and callisto-cli\\\", \\\"task_ids\\\": [\\\"M-003\\\"]}\\n+    {\\\"batch_id\\\": \\\"M-B1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Atomic typed authority cutover\\\", \\\"target_crate\\\": \\\"callisto-graph\\\", \\\"task_ids\\\": [\\\"M-001\\\"]},\\n+    {\\\"batch_id\\\": \\\"M-B2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Release-boundary propagation and final gate\\\", \\\"target_crate\\\": \\\"callisto-graph and callisto-cli\\\", \\\"task_ids\\\": [\\\"M-002\\\"]}\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[79] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[80] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n '^ci|ci-fast|test-setup-actions|audit' justfile\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":4000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[81] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\n3:default: ci-fast\n79:audit:\n80:    moon run :audit\n191:ci: fmt-check lint test audit doc-check wasm-check coverage\n199:ci-fast: fmt-check lint test audit doc-check wasm-check\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[82] tool wait_agent call: {\"timeout_ms\":10000}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[83] tool wait_agent result: {\"message\":\"Wait timed out.\",\"timed_out\":true}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[84] tool wait_agent call: {\"timeout_ms\":10000}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[85] tool wait_agent result: {\"message\":\"Wait timed out.\",\"timed_out\":true}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[86] tool send_message call: {\"target\":\"/root/correct_product_convergence_plans\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[87] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk jq '.tasks[] | {id,title,depends_on,files,steps,covers_criteria}' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":24000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[88] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"id\": \"ORCH-001\",\n  \"title\": \"Route workflow shell contracts through Just and CI\",\n  \"depends_on\": null,\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \"Justfile\",\n      \".github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"create\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_workflow_task_runner.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_workflow_task_runner.sh\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Replace legacy workflow assertions for one-day retention, Environment policy, persisted checkout credentials, and shell-built release effects with consumer-boundary assertions as later tasks land.\",\n    \"Add focused Just recipes for release-workflow contracts, release-action contracts, rehearsal topology, and recovery; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint for that contract.\",\n    \"Make the CI workflow-contracts job invoke those Just recipes after installing Just, while retaining actionlint, zizmor, and immutable action-pin checks separately.\",\n    \"Add a task-runner contract proving CI names Just recipes instead of direct release shell tests and that each recipe selects its checked-in script.\",\n    \"Run `just fmt-check`, `just lint`, and the focused release-workflow Just recipe; expect no direct release shell-contract command in CI.\"\n  ],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-014\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"ORCH-002\",\n  \"title\": \"Accept only merge-provenance and exact historical handoffs\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"ORCH-001\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\",\n      \"Justfile\"\n    ],\n    \"create\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_handoff_intake.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_handoff_intake.sh\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-work\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"3181\" /\u003e\"docs/06-publishing.md\",\n      \"Justfile\"\n    ],\n    \"create\": [\n      \".github/rehearsal/tests/test_candidate_revision_gate.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \".github/rehearsal/tests/test_candidate_revision_gate.sh\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Keep automatic production triggering disabled and keep the Environment gate until ORCH-006 evidence and all qualified prerequisite gates pass. Development remains limited to isolated branch/rehearsal routes before this activation change.\",\n    \"Make rehearsal emit activation evidence bound to exact candidate source/workflow revision, staging repository/product binding, immutable intent and artifact-manifest digests, complete upstream receipt, PM-007 final-byte verification, failpoint suite, and workflow contract suite. Production must verify every binding against its candidate and named staging evidence; another revision, repository, intent, artifact digest, or changed boundary fails closed.\",\n    \"Invalidate evidence for any prerequisite-owned schema, provider adapter, DAG, product matrix, payload verifier, attestation policy, or handoff contract change and require rehearsal of that exact revision. Production consumes evidence only and never reconstructs receipt, observation, tag, or product identity in YAML.\",\n    \"Only in this reviewed activation change remove `environment-policy`, reviewer API checks, protected Environment reviewer use, and `environment: release`; retain ORCH-004's least-privilege split, one execute invocation, and final read-only receipt validation.\",\n    \"Run the candidate-revision, workflow-contract, action-pin, rehearsal, and PM-007 Just recipes, then `just ci` and `just wasm-check`; expect automatic production eligibility only for the exact rehearsed candidate with no second human approval or widened earlier permission.\"\n  ],\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-001\",\n    \"AC-003\",\n    \"AC-008\",\n    \"AC-012\",\n    \"AC-014\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[89] assistant: Agent message from /root/correct_product_convergence_plans:\nMessage Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/correct_product_convergence_plans\nPayload:\nRevised only the two assigned plan files. Validated both schemas, unchanged spec hashes, all 24 criteria, and 14 task dependencies without cycles.\n\nDependency sequence:\n\n`PM1 → PM2 → T1`, with `PM3` and `T2` independent; then one atomic cutover `PM4 → PM5 → T3 → T3-DISPATCH → T4 → T5`; then `PM7` and `T6`; finally `PM6`.\n\nAdded exact-byte registry dispatch, full fixture classification/parser propagation, final native payload verification, and exact release WASM sandbox testing. Orchestration must invoke PM7’s verifier recipes.\n\nCargo upload and npm tarball choices were checked against [Cargo’s publish protocol](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/registry-web-api.html#publish) and [npm publish documentation](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/commands/npm-publish/).\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[90] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Justfile\\\",\\n+        \\\"justfile\\\",\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Replace legacy workflow assertions for one-day retention, Environment policy, persisted checkout credentials, and shell-built release effects with consumer-boundary assertions as later tasks land.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Before any release-boundary replacement, add a fail-closed production activation check whose initial state cannot pass; automatic production release remains disabled until ORCH-008 receives exact-candidate rehearsal evidence.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Remove the Environment reviewer gate and its policy checks while production is disabled by the activation check; the reviewed release-PR merge remains the sole eventual human approval and no temporary second approval is retained.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Replace legacy workflow assertions for one-day retention, persisted checkout credentials, and shell-built release effects with consumer-boundary assertions as later tasks land.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"covers_criteria\\\": [\\n-        \\\"AC-014\\\"\\n-      ]\\n+      \\\"covers_criteria\\\": [\\n+        \\\"AC-001\\\",\\n+        \\\"AC-012\\\",\\n+        \\\"AC-014\\\"\\n+      ]\\n@@\\n-      \\\"Justfile\\\"\\n+      \\\"justfile\\\"\\n@@\\n-    \\\"Do not begin consumer cutover until PM-004 then PM-005 then convergence T3, T4, and T5 have passed their gates, and workspace-authority M-001 through M-003 are gated. Consume their released planner, validation, ProductReleaseId, manifest, and receipt CLI interfaces without model or graph changes.\\\",\\n+    \\\"Do not begin consumer cutover until PM-004 then PM-005 then convergence T3, T3-DISPATCH, T4, and T5 have passed their gates, and workspace-authority M-001 and M-002 are gated. Consume their released planner, validation, ProductReleaseId, manifest, and receipt CLI interfaces without model or graph changes.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"Justfile\\\"\\n+      \\\"justfile\\\"\\n\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"5\" /\u003e\"Run upstream final read-only observation/receipt validation after execute, require a complete receipt for the same intent digest, and upload safe receipt/diagnostics on success or failure when available. Keep the current Environment gate until ORCH-008's activation change.\\\",\\n+    \\\"Run upstream final read-only observation/receipt validation after execute, require a complete receipt for the same intent digest, and upload safe receipt/diagnostics on success or failure when available. Keep ORCH-001's fail-closed production activation check until ORCH-008; no Environment reviewer gate exists.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"Justfile\\\"\\n+      \\\"justfile\\\"\\n@@\\n-      \\\"Justfile\\\"\\n+      \\\"justfile\\\"\\n@@\\n-      \\\"Justfile\\\"\\n+      \\\"justfile\\\"\\n@@\\n-    \\\"Keep automatic production triggering disabled and keep the Environment gate until ORCH-006 evidence and all qualified prerequisite gates pass. Development remains limited to isolated branch/rehearsal routes before this activation change.\\\",\\n+    \\\"Keep automatic production triggering disabled by ORCH-001's fail-closed activation check until ORCH-006 evidence and all qualified prerequisite gates pass. No Environment reviewer gate exists; development remains limited to isolated branch/rehearsal routes before this activation change.\\\",\\n@@\\n-    \\\"Only in this reviewed activation change remove `environment-policy`, reviewer API checks, protected Environment reviewer use, and `environment: release`; retain ORCH-004's least-privilege split, one execute invocation, and final read-only receipt validation.\\\",\\n+    \\\"Enable the reviewed automatic production route only after exact-candidate evidence validates; retain ORCH-001's assertions that `environment-policy`, reviewer API checks, protected Environment reviewer use, and `environment: release` are absent, plus ORCH-004's least-privilege split, one execute invocation, and final read-only receipt validation.\\\",\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[91] tool exec result: Script failed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n\nScript error:\napply_patch verification failed: Failed to find expected lines in /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:\n        \"Justfile\",\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[92] tool exec call: