ease-workflow-contract.sh\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Add focused Just recipes for release-workflow contracts, release-action contracts, rehearsal topology, and recovery; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint for that contract.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Add focused Just recipes only for the release-workflow and release-action contracts that already exist in this batch; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint. ORCH-005 and ORCH-006 add rehearsal and recovery recipes atomically with their scripts.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"commit_message\\\": \\\"test(ci): route release workflow contracts through just\\\",\\n+      \\\"commit_message\\\": \\\"test(ci): disable production and route release contracts through just\\\",\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005:S-001\\\"],\\n       \\\"covers_criteria\\\": [\\\"AC-001\\\", \\\"AC-012\\\", \\\"AC-014\\\"]\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5\\\", \\\"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"],\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-002\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\\\"],\\n@@\\n         \\\"Give execute only the convergence-required job-scoped permissions, expose registry secrets only to its final CLI process, invoke execute exactly once with explicit intent, artifact handoff, final bytes, checksums, attestations, source, and repository bindings, and prohibit s\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"229\" /\u003epublishing.md\\\", \\\"docs/release-paradigms.md\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n+        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/plan_publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/filter_plan.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/tag.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs\\\", \\\"docs/00-design.md\\\", \\\"docs/01-spec.md\\\", \\\"docs/06-publishing.md\\\", \\\"docs/release-paradigms.md\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Inventory action, workflow, documentation, and task-runner references to `plan-publish`, `publish`, `tag --plan`, and `filter-plan`; remove independent orchestration dispatches and contradictory guidance. CLI/model command retirement itself remains owned by the product/convergence cutover, not this consumer plan.\\\",\\n+        \\\"After the canonical release planner/executor cutover, inventory and delete every `plan-publish`, `publish`, `tag --plan`, and `filter-plan` command variant, main.rs dispatch arm, CLI args type, command module/export, graph publish/tag effect function, obsolete PublishPlan/PublishReport schema/render path, test fixture, action/workflow route and contradictory documentation. This task owns deletion only and adds no replacement release semantics.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-006\\\", \\\"ORCH-007\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-006\\\", \\\"ORCH-007\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[66] tool exec result: Script failed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\nScript error:\napply_patch verification failed: Failed to find expected lines in /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:\n        \"Give execute only the convergence-required job-scoped permissions, expose registry secrets only to its final CLI process, invoke execute exactly once with explicit intent, artifact handoff, final bytes, checksums, attestations, source, and repository bindings, and prohibit shell publishing, tagging, upload, already-present classification, or completion decisions.\",\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[67] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk sed -n '18,180p' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":26000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[68] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n      \"id\": \"ORCH-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Route workflow shell contracts through Just and CI\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\"justfile\", \".github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\", \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"],\n        \"create\": [\".github/tests/test_release_workflow_task_runner.sh\"],\n        \"test\": [\".github/tests/test_release_workflow_task_runner.sh\", \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"]\n      },\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Before any release-boundary replacement, add a fail-closed production activation check whose initial state cannot pass; automatic production release remains disabled until ORCH-008 receives exact-candidate rehearsal evidence.\",\n        \"Remove the Environment reviewer gate and its policy checks while production is disabled by the activation check; the reviewed release-PR merge remains the sole eventual human approval and no temporary second approval is retained.\",\n        \"Replace legacy workflow assertions for one-day retention, persisted checkout credentials, and shell-built release effects with consumer-boundary assertions as later tasks land.\",\n        \"Add focused Just recipes for release-workflow contracts, release-action contracts, rehearsal topology, and recovery; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint for that contract.\",\n        \"Make the CI workflow-contracts job invoke those Just recipes after installing Just, while retaining actionlint, zizmor, and immutable action-pin checks separately.\",\n        \"Add a task-runner contract proving CI names Just recipes instead of direct release shell tests and that each recipe selects its checked-in script.\",\n        \"Run `just fmt-check`, `just lint`, and the focused release-workflow Just recipe; expect no direct release shell-contract command in CI.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(ci): route release workflow contracts through just\",\n\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"3621\" /\u003eract suite. Production must verify every binding against its candidate and named staging evidence; another revision, repository, intent, artifact digest, or changed boundary fails closed.\",\n        \"Invalidate evidence for any prerequisite-owned schema, provider adapter, DAG, product matrix, payload verifier, attestation policy, or handoff contract change and require rehearsal of that exact revision. Production consumes evidence only and never reconstructs receipt, observation, tag, or product identity in YAML.\",\n        \"Enable the reviewed automatic production route only after exact-candidate evidence validates; retain ORCH-001's assertions that `environment-policy`, reviewer API checks, protected Environment reviewer use, and `environment: release` are absent, plus ORCH-004's least-privilege split, one execute invocation, and final read-only receipt validation.\",\n        \"Run the candidate-revision, workflow-contract, action-pin, rehearsal, and PM-007 Just recipes, then `just ci` and `just wasm-check`; expect automatic production eligibility only for the exact rehearsed candidate with no second human approval or widened earlier permission.\"\n      ],\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(ci): gate production activation on rehearsal evidence\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"ORCH-006\", \"ORCH-007\"],\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\", \"AC-003\", \"AC-008\", \"AC-012\", \"AC-014\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\"batch_id\": \"workflow-contracts\", \"title\": \"Task-runner and immutable-handoff contracts\", \"target_crate\": \".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\", \"task_ids\": [\"ORCH-001\", \"ORCH-002\", \"ORCH-003\", \"ORCH-004\"]},\n    {\"batch_id\": \"rehearsal\", \"title\": \"Isolated rehearsal and recovery evidence\", \"target_crate\": \".github/workflows/callisto-release-rehearsal.yml\", \"task_ids\": [\"ORCH-005\", \"ORCH-006\"]},\n    {\"batch_id\": \"retirement-activation\", \"title\": \"Route retirement and production activation\", \"target_crate\": \".github\", \"task_ids\": [\"ORCH-007\", \"ORCH-008\"]}\n  ]\n}\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[69] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\"justfile\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\"],\\n+        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\"justfile\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Add focused Just recipes for release-workflow contracts, release-action contracts, rehearsal topology, and recovery; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint for that contract.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Add focused Just recipes only for release-workflow and release-action contracts that exist in this batch; each recipe invokes its checked-in shell contract and becomes the sole local/CI entrypoint. ORCH-005 and ORCH-006 add rehearsal and recovery recipes atomically with their scripts.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"commit_message\\\": \\\"test(ci): route release workflow contracts through just\\\",\\n+      \\\"commit_message\\\": \\\"test(ci): disable production and route release contracts through just\\\",\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005:S-001\\\"],\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5\\\", \\\"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"],\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-002\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\\\"],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[70] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 6.6 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[71] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n         \\\"Give execute only the convergence-required job-scoped permissions, expose registry secrets only to its final CLI process, invoke execute exactly once with explicit intent, artifact directory, state path, and receipt path, and prohibit shell publishing, tagging, upload, already-present classification, or completion decisions.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Obtain a canonical concurrency key only from the CLI's revalidated repository identity plus ProductReleaseId and expose it as a validation-job output. Apply that exact key to the credentialed execute job for both managed-merge and workflow_dispatch recovery routes with cancel-in-progress=false; YAML must not reconstruct it from github.ref, branch names, inputs or tag strings.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-004\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-004\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-006\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Consume convergence T6's failpoint interface and diagnostics only. For every exposed post-mutation/pre-journal-or-receipt failpoint, stop rehearsal and resume in a different job or workflow run with no predecessor `RUNNER_TEMP`; do not create provider observers, mutations, journal logic, receipt writing, or a shell recovery algorithm.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Consume convergence T5-FAILPOINT's failpoint interface and T6's diagnostics only. For every exposed post-mutation/pre-journal-or-receipt failpoint, stop rehearsal and resume in a different job or workflow run with no predecessor `RUNNER_TEMP`; do not create provider observers, mutations, journal logic, receipt writing, or a shell recovery algorithm.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-005\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-005\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5-FAILPOINT\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T6\\\"],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[72] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 29.0 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[73] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Do not begin until PM-007 is implemented after the PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5 cutover. Reuse PM-007's `build-release-payload`, `verify-release-payload`, `test-release-payload-verification`, and `test-release-wasm-payload` recipes and its exact Moon sandbox WASM path/SHA-256 contract; do not add a parallel archive, smoke-test, checksum, or WASM verifier.\\\",\\n-        \\\"Obtain the total matrix solely from the validated immutable intent, fan out exactly the emitted entries, return them to fan-in, and invoke the product-owned final-byte verifier there and again before execute. Shell must not enumerate the four product targets, registry artifacts, slots, archive names, checksum rules, or manifest fields.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Do not begin until PM-008 is implemented after PM-007 and the PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5 cutover. Invoke only PM-008's build-matrix, build-slot and assemble-artifacts CLI plus PM-007's verifier recipes; do not add a parallel packager, archive rule, smoke test, checksum, manifest assembler or WASM verifier.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Obtain the total matrix solely from `callisto release build-matrix --intent`, fan out exactly those entries, and invoke build-slot. On each matching native/WASM runner run PM-007 platform-local verification and return its digest-bound evidence with the final bytes. Fan-in and pre-execute use PM-007 portable verification to rehash bytes and validate the complete evidence roster; they never attempt foreign-architecture native execution.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Invoke PM-008 assemble-artifacts only after all slot reports and platform-local evidence arrive. Shell must not enumerate the four product targets, registry artifacts, slots, builder kinds, archive names, metadata fields, checksum rules or manifest fields.\\\",\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Run `just build-release-payload`, `just verify-release-payload`, `just test-release-payload-verification`, `just test-release-wasm-payload`, the build-handoff Just recipe, `just fmt-check`, and `just lint`; expect intent-driven fan-out, retained handoffs, attestation transport, and no product roster or byte verifier in workflow shell.\\\"\\n+        \\\"Run the PM-008 CLI contract tests, `just test-release-payload-verification`, `just test-release-wasm-payload`, the build-handoff Just recipe, `just fmt-check`, and `just lint`; expect intent-driven fan-out, platform-local evidence, portable fan-in/pre-execute validation, retained handoffs, attestation transport, and no product roster or build semantics in workflow shell.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[74] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 6.9 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[75] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\"docs/00-design.md\\\", \\\"docs/01-spec.md\\\", \\\"docs/06-publishing.md\\\", \\\"docs/release-paradigms.md\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n+        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\\\", \\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/plan_publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/filter_plan.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/tag.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/mod.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/plan.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs\\\", \\\"docs/00-design.md\\\", \\\"docs/01-spec.md\\\", \\\"docs/06-publishing.md\\\", \\\"docs/release-paradigms.md\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Inventory action, workflow, documentation, and task-runner references to `plan-publish`, `publish`, `tag --plan`, and `filter-plan`; remove independent orchestration dispatches and contradictory guidance. CLI/model command retirement itself remains owned by the product/convergence cutover, not this consumer plan.\\\",\\n+        \\\"After the canonical release planner/executor cutover, inventory and delete every `plan-publish`, `publish`, `tag --plan`, and `filter-plan` command variant, main.rs dispatch arm, CLI args type, command module/export, graph publish/tag effect function, obsolete PublishPlan/PublishReport schema/render path, test fixture, action/workflow route and contradictory documentation. This task owns deletion only and adds no replacement release semantics.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-006\\\", \\\"ORCH-007\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-006\\\", \\\"ORCH-007\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[76] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 5.6 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[77] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-        \\\"test\\\": [\\\".github/tests/test_release_route_retirement.sh\\\"]\\n+        \\\"test\\\": [\\\".github/tests/test_release_route_retirement.sh\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/cmd/help.trycmd\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/lifecycle_e2e_tests.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/subprocess_dispatch_and_stdin_tests.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/dry_run_invariant_tests.rs\\\"]\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[78] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 5.7 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[79] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.json\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002\\\"],\\n@@\\n-  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Cross-plan dependencies use \u003clinked_spec\u003e:\u003ctask_id\u003e, resolving to that persisted plan's task, never whole-plan completion. Executable order: PM-001 -\u003e PM-002; PM-003 independently; convergence T1 follows PM-002 and T2 is independent. Then ONE indivisible workspace compilation/commit boundary CUTOVER-1 runs PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5, with T1/T2 already complete. PM-004/005 intermediate edits are not runnable/checkpoint commits; their commit_message values describe the joint commit scopes. No passing workspace gate is claimed until T5 runs just fmt-check, just lint, just test and just wasm-check across all immediate consumers. Afterwards PM-007 produces platform-local/portable payload evidence, PM-008 owns the complete credential-free matrix/build/manifest producer, and convergence T6 runs before PM-006's final gate. There is no edge from a convergence foundation/cutover task to PM-006 or to whole-plan completion. PM-001/002 stage private domain construction/validation additions without changing existing public signatures or accepting a second durable wire format; CUTOVER-1 replaces old production types and removes all old constructors/decoders in the same change. Live affected Rust inventory: model release.rs; graph release.rs, release_artifacts.rs, release_execution.rs, release_store.rs and commands/mod.rs; CLI commands/release.rs plus CLI help/tests. The architecture model assigns those roles downward through model -\u003e graph -\u003e CLI, with vcs owning Git. Receipt/evidence work stays exclusively with convergence even where model release.rs is shared. AC-006 publication of verified bytes is completed by convergence T3-DISPATCH; AC-008's full obser\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"124\" /\u003eace compilation/commit boundary CUTOVER-1 runs PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5, with T1/T2 and baseline BR-002 already complete. PM-004/005 intermediate edits are not runnable/checkpoint commits; their commit_message values describe the joint commit scopes. No passing workspace gate is claimed until T5 runs just fmt-check, just lint, just test and just wasm-check across all immediate consumers. Afterwards PM-007 produces platform-local/portable payload evidence, PM-008 owns the complete credential-free matrix/build/manifest producer, and convergence T6 runs before PM-006's final gate. There is no edge from a convergence foundation/cutover task to PM-006 or to whole-plan completion. PM-001/002 stage private domain construction/validation additions without changing existing public signatures or accepting a second durable wire format; CUTOVER-1 replaces old production types and removes all old constructors/decoders in the same change. Live affected Rust inventory: model release.rs; graph release.rs, release_artifacts.rs, release_execution.rs, release_store.rs and commands/mod.rs; CLI commands/release.rs plus CLI help/tests. The architecture model assigns those roles downward through model -\u003e graph -\u003e CLI, with vcs owning Git. Receipt/evidence work stays exclusively with convergence even where model release.rs is shared. AC-006 publication of verified bytes is completed by convergence T3-DISPATCH; AC-008's full observer/dispatch gate runs only in PM-006 after convergence T6. AC-005 verifier implementation is PM-007 and complete artifact production is PM-008; orchestration invokes those owned interfaces rather than recreating them.\\\"\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json\\n@@\\n       \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\n-        \\\"T3\\\"\\n+        \\\"T3\\\",\\n+        \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"\\n       ],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[80] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time