by convergence T3-DISPATCH; AC-008's full obser\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"124\" /\u003eace compilation/commit boundary CUTOVER-1 runs PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5, with T1/T2 and baseline BR-002 already complete. PM-004/005 intermediate edits are not runnable/checkpoint commits; their commit_message values describe the joint commit scopes. No passing workspace gate is claimed until T5 runs just fmt-check, just lint, just test and just wasm-check across all immediate consumers. Afterwards PM-007 produces platform-local/portable payload evidence, PM-008 owns the complete credential-free matrix/build/manifest producer, and convergence T6 runs before PM-006's final gate. There is no edge from a convergence foundation/cutover task to PM-006 or to whole-plan completion. PM-001/002 stage private domain construction/validation additions without changing existing public signatures or accepting a second durable wire format; CUTOVER-1 replaces old production types and removes all old constructors/decoders in the same change. Live affected Rust inventory: model release.rs; graph release.rs, release_artifacts.rs, release_execution.rs, release_store.rs and commands/mod.rs; CLI commands/release.rs plus CLI help/tests. The architecture model assigns those roles downward through model -\u003e graph -\u003e CLI, with vcs owning Git. Receipt/evidence work stays exclusively with convergence even where model release.rs is shared. AC-006 publication of verified bytes is completed by convergence T3-DISPATCH; AC-008's full observer/dispatch gate runs only in PM-006 after convergence T6. AC-005 verifier implementation is PM-007 and complete artifact production is PM-008; orchestration invokes those owned interfaces rather than recreating them.\\\"\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json\\n@@\\n       \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\n-        \\\"T3\\\"\\n+        \