callisto-moon on RUSTSEC-2026-0285 via rustls 0.23.43 and yanked chacha20 0.10.1; the initial sandbox-only advisory DB lock failure was separately eliminated with authorized audit access.\\\"\\n+  },\\n+  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n+  \\\"spec_file_path\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"plan_file_path\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"spec_drift_warning\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"plan_drift_warning\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"workflow_provenance\\\": [\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"navigator\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.3.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"scribe\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"3.3.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"smith\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.4.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"sentinel\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.1.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"ranger\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"3.2.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"vanguard\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.0.2\\\"},\\n+    {\\\"plugin\\\": \\\"weaver\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"3.0.3\\\"}\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This combined manifest covers the independent first implementation wave. Each implementer still receives its exact spec/plan paths and criteria; shared interface decisions and final verification remain with the primary agent.\\\"\\n+}\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[80] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 7.3 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[81] assistant: Agent message from /root/plan_adversary_round2:\nMessage Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan_adversary_round2\nPayload:\nScoped recheck: fail on three remaining ownership/order issues. The other named corrections pass.\n\n1. Cross-plan shared edits remain unordered. After T5, ORCH-002 and PM-007 can both edit `justfile`. After PM-008, ORCH-003 and S-002 can both edit it. S-004 also remains unordered against orchestration edits to `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh`. Add dependency edges or an explicit sequential owner for these edits.\n\n2. ORCH-007 can overlap PM-006. ORCH-007 deletes CLI render/model/graph surfaces while PM-006 modifies release presentation and architecture coverage. ORCH-007 currently depends only on ORCH-004; add PM-006 as a prerequisite.\n\n3. The concurrency-key producer remains incompletely assigned. ORCH-004 specifies consuming a CLI-derived repository/ProductReleaseId key and permits a thin CLI output adapter, but lists no CLI files. No upstream task explicitly produces that key. Assign the adapter, exact CLI files, and an output-contract test.\n\nVerified corrections: PM-008 owns matrix/build/assembly; PM-004 owns production/rehearsal bindings; T5-FAILPOINT owns the executor/CLI interface and T6 drives it; ORCH-007 owns legacy route deletion; PM-007 separates native evidence from portable validation; ORCH-001 owns the release workflow and creates recipes with scripts; baseline audit bypasses cache; S-002’s oracle and pnpm 12.x semantics are corrected.\n\nAll twelve artifacts pass JSON Schema validation. All six spec hashes match, criterion-ID coverage is complete, and the declared dependency graph has no cycles or unresolved task IDs.\n\nSafe immediate batches:\n\n- Product `B1-additive-product-contract`.\n- Membership `M-B1`.\n- Baseline `BR-B1`.\n- Setup `S-B1`.\n- Convergence T2 individually; its full foundation batch requires PM-002.\n\nPM’s fixture-classification batch now correctly waits for membership M-002.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[82] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005.json\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"S-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"S-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003:ORCH-001\\\"],\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5\\\", \\\"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-001\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5\\\", \\\"SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\\\", \\\"SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005:S-004\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n+        \\\"modify\\\": [\\\".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs\\\", \\\"justfile\\\"],\\n@@\\n-        \\\"test\\\": [\\\".github/tests/test_release_execute_boundary.sh\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\"]\\n+        \\\"test\\\": [\\\".github/tests/test_release_execute_boundary.sh\\\", \\\".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\\\", \\\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/release_workflow_bindings_tests.rs\\\"]\\n@@\\n-        \\\"Obtain a canonical concurrency key only from the CLI's revalidated repository identity plus ProductReleaseId and expose it as a validation-job output. Apply that exact key to the credentialed execute job for both managed-merge and workflow_dispatch recovery routes with cancel-in-progress=false; YAML must not reconstruct it from github.ref, branch names, inputs or tag strings.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Add a thin `callisto release workflow-bindings --intent --expect-repository` CLI adapter returning strict JSON `{ repository, product_release_id, concurrency_key }` only after normal intent and repository revalidation. Define concurrency_key as a safe canonical encoding of those two validated fields, with no tag parsing or workflow-supplied component; add process tests for exact output, unsafe repository input, mismatched intent and automatic/manual identity equality.\\\",\\n+        \\\"Expose that exact CLI concurrency_key as a validation-job output and apply it unchanged to the credentialed execute job for both managed-merge and workflow_dispatch recovery routes with cancel-in-progress=false; YAML must not reconstruct it from github.ref, branch names, inputs or tag strings.\\\",\\n@@\\n-      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-004\\\"],\\n+      \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"ORCH-004\\\", \\\"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-006\\\"],\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[83] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 4.8 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[84] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk jq empty docs/projects/*.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq -r '.tasks[]|.id+\\\" \u003c- \\\"+((.depends_on//[])|join(\\\",\\\"))' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq -r '.tasks[]|.id+\\\" \u003c- \\\"+((.depends_on//[])|join(\\\",\\\"))' docs/projects/SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":8000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[85] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n\nORCH-001 \u003c- SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005:S-001\nORCH-002 \u003c- ORCH-001,SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5,SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004:M-002,SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002,SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005:S-004\nORCH-003 \u003c- ORCH-002,SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\nORCH-004 \u003c- ORCH-003\nORCH-005 \u003c- ORCH-004,SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-006\nORCH-006 \u003c- ORCH-005,SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T5-FAILPOINT,SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002:T6\nORCH-007 \u003c- ORCH-004,SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-006\nORCH-008 \u003c- ORCH-006,ORCH-007,SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006:BR-002\n\nS-001 \u003c- \nS-002 \u003c- S-001,SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008,SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003:ORCH-001\nS-003 \u003c- S-002\nS-004 \u003c- S-003\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[86] tool followup_task call: {\"target\":\"/root/plan_adversary_round2\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[87] assistant: The plan graph is now executable and the first implementation wave is beginning in the isolated worktree. I’m assigning two fixed-interface Smith batches in parallel—workspace authority and the immutable setup resolver—while I handle the dependency-audit baseline. Each worker owns disjoint files, cannot commit or touch release providers, and must return exact test evidence; the product-model batch will start as soon as the final graph recheck frees a slot.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[88] tool spawn_agent call: {\"task_name\":\"implement_membership_m1\",\"fork_turns\":\"none\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"high\",\"agent_type\":\"worker\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[89] tool spawn_agent result: {\"task_name\":\"/root/implement_membership_m1\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[90] tool spawn_agent call: {\"task_name\":\"implement_setup_s1\",\"fork_turns\":\"none\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"high\",\"agent_type\":\"worker\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[91] tool spawn_agent result: {\"task_name\":\"/root/implement_setup_s1\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[92] assistant: Agent message from /root/plan_adversary_round2:\nMessage Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan_adversary_round2\nPayload:\nFail. No cycles or unresolved task IDs, but two blockers remain:\n\n- ORCH-004 still omits `crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs` and `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs` from `files.modify`; its new test appears only under `test`, not `create`.\n- ORCH-001 and PM-007 remain unordered despite both modifying `justfile`. S-002 waiting for both does not serialize them. Add ORCH-001 as a PM-007 dependency.\n\nThe other scoped corrections pass.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[93] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk jq '.tasks[]|select(.id==\\\"ORCH-003\\\" or .id==\\\"ORCH-004\\\")|{id,files,depends_on}' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq '.tasks[]|select(.id==\\\"PM-007\\\")|{id,depends_on}' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":8000}); text(r.output)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[94] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"id\": \"ORCH-003\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs\",\n      \"justfile\"\n    ],\n    \"create\": [\n      \".github/actions/build-release-artifacts/action.yml\",\n      \".github/actions/build-release-artifacts/scripts/build-from-intent.sh\",\n      \".github/actions/build-release-artifacts/tests/test_build_handoff_contract.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \".github/actions/build-release-artifacts/tests/test_build_handoff_contract.sh\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"ORCH-002\",\n    \"SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001:PM-008\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"ORCH-004\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"modify\": [\n      \".github/workflows/callisto-release.yml\",\n      \".github/tests/verify-release-workflow-contract.sh\",\n      \"justfile\"\n    ],\n    \"create\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_execute_boundary.sh\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": [\n      \".github/tests/test_release_execute_boundary.sh\",\n   