tions v2.2.0\n    Checking icu_locale_core v2.2.0\n    Checking gix-shallow v0.13.0\nerror: public documentation for `parse` links to private item `is_valid_git_ref_name`\n   --\u003e crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs:176:11\n    |\n176 |     /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]) plus a leading `-`, which is a legal Git\n    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this item is private\n    |\n    = note: this link will resolve properly if you pass `--document-private-items`\n    = note: `-D rustdoc::private-intra-doc-links` implied by `-D warnings`\n    = help: to override `-D warnings` add `#[allow(rustdoc::private_intra_doc_links)]`\n\nerror: public documentation for `new_unchecked` links to private item `is_valid_git_ref_name`\n   --\u003e crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs:188:11\n    |\n188 |     /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]. Restricted to call sites that can prove\n    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this item is private\n    |\n    = note: this link will resolve properly if you pass `--document-private-items`\n\nerror: could not document `callisto-model`\nwarning: build failed, waiting for other jobs to finish...\nerror: recipe `doc-check` failed on line 114 with exit code 101\n\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[87] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk git diff -- crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs \u0026\u0026 rtk git show HEAD:crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs | rtk rg -n 'is_valid_git_ref_name'\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[88] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n\n57:        if !is_valid_git_ref_name(\u0026test_render) {\n78:        // Unchecked: `prefix`/`suffix` already passed `is_valid_git_ref_name`\n137:fn is_valid_git_ref_name(s: \u0026str) -\u003e bool {\n176:    /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]) plus a leading `-`, which is a legal Git\n180:        if is_valid_git_ref_name(s) {\n188:    /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]. Restricted to call sites that can prove\n420:    fn is_valid_git_ref_name_rejects_dotdot_and_at_brace() {\n421:        assert!(!is_valid_git_ref_name(\"v1..2\"), \"'..' must be rejected\");\n422:        assert!(!is_valid_git_ref_name(\"v1@{2\"), \"'@{{' must be rejected\");\n426:    fn is_valid_git_ref_name_rejects_lock_suffixed_and_leading_dot_components() {\n428:            !is_valid_git_ref_name(\"refs/heads/v1.lock\"),\n432:            !is_valid_git_ref_name(\"refs/.hidden/v1\"),\n438:    fn is_valid_git_ref_name_rejects_control_and_reserved_characters() {\n439:        assert!(!is_valid_git_ref_name(\"v1\\t2\"), \"a control character must be rejected\");\n440:        assert!(!is_valid_git_ref_name(\"v1 2\"), \"a space must be rejected\");\n444:                !is_valid_git_ref_name(\u0026candidate),\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[89] assistant: The post-fix test, format, and clippy gates are green. Documentation checking exposed a second baseline failure unrelated to this wave: two public doc comments in unchanged `tag.rs` link to a private helper, and `-D warnings` rejects them. This exists in the branch base; I’m checking the baseline-readiness plan before deciding whether it belongs in this recovery wave or should remain a separately tracked blocker.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[90] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk jq '{spec:.metadata,criteria:.criteria}' docs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq '.tasks // .plan // .' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-BASELINE-READINESS-006.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[91] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"spec\": null,\n  \"criteria\": null\n}\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"BR-001\",\n    \"title\": \"Resolve the two confirmed dependency-policy failures minimally\",\n    \"files\": {\n      \"modify\": [\n        \"Cargo.lock\",\n        \"Cargo.toml\",\n        \"crates/callisto-moon/Cargo.toml\"\n      ],\n      \"test\": [\n        \"Cargo.lock\",\n        \"deny.toml\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"Record `cargo tree -i rustls@0.23.43` and `cargo tree -i chacha20@0.10.1` before mutation to identify every direct and transitive constraint; do not edit deny.toml.\",\n      \"Use the smallest compatible Cargo resolver update that selects rustls \u003e=0.23.45 and a non-yanked chacha20; change a direct manifest constraint only when the resolver proves the lockfile alone cannot satisfy the criterion.\",\n      \"Inspect the complete Cargo.lock delta and revert unrelated resolver movement by tightening the update command or direct constraint; document every package that must move with the two target paths.\",\n      \"Run `cargo tree -i rustls` and `cargo tree -i chacha20`; expect all selected rustls versions to be \u003e=0.23.45 and no chacha20 0.10.1 node.\",\n      \"Run `just test`; expect all workspace tests, including callisto-moon tests, to pass.\"\n    ],\n    \"commit_message\": \"fix(deps): restore release audit baseline\",\n    \"covers_criteria\": [\n      \"AC-001\",\n      \"AC-002\",\n      \"AC-003\",\n      \"AC-004\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"BR-002\",\n    \"title\": \"Verify the current audit and Moon/WASM boundary\",\n    \"files\": {\n      \"test\": [\n        \"Cargo.lock\",\n        \"crates/callisto-moon/tests/moon_wasm_sandbox.rs\",\n        \"deny.toml\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"Run the project-native focused Moon test task through `just test`; expect the Moon/Extism sandbox and all callisto-moon unit/integration tests to pass.\",\n      \"Run `just wasm-check`; expect callisto-moon to compile for wasm32-wasip1 with the configured PDK feature.\",\n      \"Run `rtk env MOON_FORCE=true just audit` with a current reachable advisory database, bypassing Moon's input cache because advisory state is external to its hash; expect zero vulnerability and yanked-version failures and record verification time plus advisory database fetch or revision evidence.\",\n      \"Run `just ci`; expect formatting, lint, workspace tests, doc tests, and audit to pass, then retain the forced-audit result as the authoritative current-advisory evidence. If advisory-database access is sandbox-blocked, rerun only the forced audit with authorized database access and report the environmental split explicitly.\",\n      \"Deliberate-fault check: evaluate the pre-update Cargo.lock with the same current audit database or otherwise retain the observed baseline output; expect it to fail on RUSTSEC-2026-0285 and yanked chacha20 0.10.1 while the corrected lock passes.\"\n    ],\n    \"commit_message\": \"test(deps): verify Moon release readiness\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"BR-001\"\n    ],\n    \"covers_criteria\": [\n      \"AC-001\",\n      \"AC-002\",\n      \"AC-003\",\n      \"AC-004\",\n      \"AC-005\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[92] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs\\n@@\\n-    /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]) plus a leading `-`, which is a legal Git\\n+    /// `is_valid_git_ref_name`) plus a leading `-`, which is a legal Git\\n@@\\n-    /// [`is_valid_git_ref_name`]. Restricted to call sites that can prove\\n+    /// `is_valid_git_ref_name`. Restricted to call sites that can prove\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[93] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 6.3 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[94] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk just doc-check\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","type