 \"ring\",\n@@ -6857,7 +6857,7 @@ source = \"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\"\n checksum = \"32497e9a4c7b38532efcdebeef879707aa9f794296a4f0244f6f69e9bc8574bd\"\n dependencies = [\n  \"fastrand\",\n- \"getrandom 0.4.3\",\n+ \"getrandom 0.3.4\",\n  \"once_cell\",\n  \"rustix 1.1.4\",\n  \"windows-sys 0.61.2\",\n  +9 -9\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[69] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n 'retention-days|environment: release|environment-policy|production-activation' .github/workflows/callisto-release.yml \u0026\u0026 rtk git diff -- Cargo.lock | rtk rg -n '^[-+]version|^[-+]name|^[-+] *\\\"getrandom|rustls|chacha|aws-lc'\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[70] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n156:          retention-days: 1\n205:          retention-days: 1\n207:  production-activation:\n223:    needs: production-activation\n10: name = \"aws-lc-rs\"\n11:-version = \"1.17.3\"\n12:+version = \"1.18.1\"\n17:  \"aws-lc-sys\",\n22: name = \"aws-lc-sys\"\n23:-version = \"0.43.0\"\n24:+version = \"0.45.0\"\n34: name = \"chacha20\"\n35:-version = \"0.10.1\"\n36:+version = \"0.10.2\"\n46: name = \"rustls\"\n47:-version = \"0.23.43\"\n48:+version = \"0.23.45\"\n53:  \"aws-lc-rs\",\n58: name = \"rustls-webpki\"\n59:-version = \"0.103.13\"\n60:+version = \"0.103.15\"\n65:  \"aws-lc-rs\",\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[71] assistant: The split is clear now: #95 conflicts with the approved model, #96 remains useful, and #97 is necessary in concept but is no longer sufficient or minimal as written. I’m checking the persisted criteria for artifact retention before giving you the merge/close recommendation.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[72] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n -i 'retention|environment|approval|artifact.*handoff|historical' docs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json docs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json | rtk head -160\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":24000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[73] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:3:  \"purpose\": \"Define a fast, single-approval GitHub workflow that builds and executes the immutable Callisto product release, supports exact historical recovery on fresh runners, and proves the complete path in an isolated rehearsal before production.\",\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:4:  \"scope\": \"Release pull request authorization, GitHub Actions jobs and permissions, plan and artifact handoffs, four-target build fan-out, manual historical recovery, removal of the Environment approval, staging-rehearsal topology and failpoints, and retirement of superseded pre-v1 release routes.\",\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:6:    \"A second human approval after the release pull request is merged.\",\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:35:      \"criterion\": \"The reviewed managed release pull request merge is the sole human approval event. The production workflow contains no environment-policy job, required-reviewer API check, protected Environment reviewer gate, or second manual approval; merge automatically proceeds through plan, build, attest, execute, and final verify when checks pass.\",\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:45:      \"criterion\": \"Planning has read-only repository permission and no release credentials. Build jobs have only source-read plus attestation/OIDC permissions. A separate read-only validation job validates the intent, source commit, complete artifact manifest, bytes, checksums, and attestations before execute starts. The execute job has job-scoped contents-write permission, repeats validation, and exposes registry secrets only to the final CLI invocation. Removing the Environment gate does not widen any earlier job's permissions.\",\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:55:      \"criterion\": \"Intent, artifact-manifest, metadata, and receipt handoffs use strict model schemas, whi\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"2525\" /\u003eronment-gated, per-package release, journal-authoritative, and shell-owned effect instructions without pre-v1 compatibility claims.\",\ndocs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:163:        \"Keep automatic production triggering disabled by ORCH-001's fail-closed activation check until ORCH-006 evidence and all qualified prerequisite gates pass. No Environment reviewer gate exists; development remains limited to isolated branch/rehearsal routes before this activation change.\",\ndocs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:166:        \"Enable the reviewed automatic production route only after exact-candidate evidence validates; retain ORCH-001's assertions that `environment-policy`, reviewer API checks, protected Environment reviewer use, and `environment: release` are absent, plus ORCH-004's least-privilege split, one execute invocation, and final read-only receipt validation.\",\ndocs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.json:167:        \"Run the candidate-revision, workflow-contract, action-pin, rehearsal, and PM-007 Just recipes, then `just ci` and `just wasm-check`; expect automatic production eligibility only for the exact rehearsed candidate with no second human approval or widened earlier permission.\"\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json:10:    \"Defining the product target roster or workflow approval policy, which are specified separately.\"\ndocs/specs/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.json:124:      \"criterion\": \"The graph-private prepared operation remains the only effect and observation input. Raw artifact manifests are accepted only by a graph validation constructor that returns a non-serializable ValidatedArtifactManifest bound to the same ValidatedReleaseIntent; converge_release accepts only that capability. Provider adapters cannot accept free-form package, version, endpoint, tag, repository, asset name, or digest values from CLI flags, workflow environment, mutable configuration, or execution state after validation.\",\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[74] assistant: Not all of them.\n\n| PR | Recommendation | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| [#95](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/95) | **Close as superseded** | It removes the policy check but retains `environment: release` and documents reviewer approval as optional. Our approved architecture requires the Environment gate and boundary to be absent entirely. |\n| [#96](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/96) | **Keep** | Seven-day artifact retention is explicitly required for exact historical recovery. This is valid independent work, although it needs refreshed checks after the audit repair. |\n| [#97](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/97) | **Keep, but amend before merging** | The `rustls` fix is required, but the PR now misses the yanked `chacha20 0.10.1` problem and includes unrelated `tempfile/getrandom` lockfile movement. Our recovery branch has the minimal combined lockfile correction. |\n\nRecommended sequence:\n\n1. Close #95.\n2. Update #97 with the minimal `rustls` + `chacha20` repair, then merge it.\n3. Rebase/refresh #96 and merge it.\n4. Rebase the recovery work onto those changes, dropping the duplicated lockfile and retention edits.\n\nI have not closed, updated, or merged anything yet.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[75] user: Can we close and ammend as necessary?\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[76] assistant: Yes. I’ll close #95 as superseded, repair #97 into the minimal combined audit fix, rerun its focused verification, and refresh #96 only if its branch needs rebasing after #97. I’m using the commit/PR workflow skills because this now involves authenticated commits and remote PR state.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[77] tool exec call: const paths=[\n\"/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/commit/SKILL.md\",\n\"/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/pr/SKILL.md\"\n];\nfor (const p of paths){const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:`rtk bat --paging=never ${p}`,workdir:\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:30000}); text(`=== ${p} ===\\n${r.output}`)}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[78] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n\n=== /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/commit/SKILL.md ===\n---\nname: commit\ndescription: Prepare or create a conventional commit from staged work. Use when the user asks to commit changes or write a commit message; never create a commit without confirmation.\n---\n\nState material concerns, evidence, consequence, and confidence directly. Do not soften blockers, manufacture praise, or claim certainty beyond the evidence.\n\n# Commit verified work\n\nInspect the staged diff, staged file list, and recent commit history before drafting anything. Do not infer scope from unstaged work or a task description when the index says otherwise.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm that the index contains the intended files and identify the smallest coherent change represented by it.\n2. Read `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` for type, scope, and voice rules.\n3. Draft a conventional commit subject and body that explains why the change exists. Let the diff carry mechanical detail.\n4. Show the exact message and staged file scope.\n5. Create the commit only after the user explicitly confirms that exact message and scope.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Do not stage, amend, reset, rebase, or commit unrelated changes unless the user explicitly asks.\n- If staged work contains unrelated topics, explain the split and ask which subset to commit rather than producing a misleading umbrella message.\n- If no changes are staged, report that fact and do not substitute the working-tree diff.\n\n## Team use\n\nThis is a bounded single-artifact task. Complete it yourself; do not request an agent team.\n\n=== /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/pr/SKILL.md ===\n---\nname: pr\ndescription: Draft or open a reviewer-ready pull request from verified work. Use when the user asks to create a PR or write its description; require confirmation before any remote action.\n---\n\nState material concerns, evidence, consequence,\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"61\" /\u003e understand the intent, evidence, and residual risk without reconstructing the branch history.\n\n## Evidence to collect\n\n- Compare the current branch to its intended base and inspect the full diff.\n- Read linked `shared/schemas/requirement@1.json`, `shared/schemas/spec@1.json`, or persisted artifact paths only when they apply to the change.\n- Record verification commands and their observed outcomes. Do not claim checks that were not run.\n- Identify migrations, operational follow-up, known limitations, and intentionally deferred work.\n\n## Draft shape\n\nWrite a concise title and body with:\n\n- An outcome-led summary of user-visible or architectural intent.\n- Observed verification with exact commands or inspections and results.\n- Reasons and coverage gaps for checks not run.\n- Risks, migrations, limitations, or follow-up only when they apply.\n- Existing issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset links only when they help review.\n\nUse enough summary bullets to explain one coherent change. If the summary reveals independent topics, recommend separate PRs or state the dependency that requires one delivery.\n\nShow the exact title, body, labels, base branch, and repository target before creating anything remotely. Create the PR only after explicit user confirmation.\n\n## Team use\n\nBefore delegating, read `agent-roles/README.md`; use `recon` for linked-criteria inventory or `reviewer` for verification-output review, never for the final PR narrative.\n\nWhen agent teams are available, use parallel work only for independent evidence collection: one teammate may inventory linked criteria while another summarizes verification output. Reconcile both against the live diff yourself. If teams are unavailable, collect those inputs sequentially and produce the same result.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Do not publish a draft as a PR, assign reviewers, add labels, or alter the target branch without user confirmation.\n- Do not fabricate issue links, test results, or acceptance evidence.\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[79] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk bat --paging=never /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/shared/references/delivery/commits.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[80] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\n\u001b[31m[bat error]\u001b[0m: '/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/skills/shared/references/delivery/commits.md': No such file or directory (os error 2)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[81] assistant: The commit skill’s referenced guidance is not at the documented relative path, so I’m locating the packaged reference before touching any branch. This pauses only the commit step; the PR-state plan remains unchanged.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[82] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk fd -t f commits.md /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[83] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/shared/references/delivery/commits.md\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[84] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk bat --paging=never /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/courier/3.0.3/shared/references/delivery/commits.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[85] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n# Conventional Commits Reference\n\n**Format:** `\u003ctype\u003e(\u003cscope\u003e): \u003cdescription\u003e`\n\nTypes: `feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `test` `chore` `perf` `ci` `build` `revert`\n\nBreaking change: append `!` after type/scope, or add `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Subject line: imperative mood, no period, under 72 characters\n- Body (optional): explain the *why*, not the what. Do not artificially wrap lines — one paragraph per line, let the terminal/renderer soft-wrap.\n- Footer: `BREAKING CHANGE: \u003cdescription\u003e`, `Fixes #123`, `Refs #456`\n- Scope is optional; when used, it names the module or component\n\n## Examples\n\n```\nfeat(courier): add changeset generation skill\n\nfix(sentinel): retry gate passes specific failure message to producer\n\ndocs(shared): add conventional-commits reference\n\nrefactor(ranger): extract language detection into recon subagent\n\nfeat!: rename bug-hunter-rust to proof\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: plugin ID changed from bug-hunter-rust to proof.\nUpdate marketplace.json and skill trigger references.\n\nfeat!: rename proof to ranger\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: plugin ID changed from proof to ranger.\nUpdate marketplace.json and skill trigger references.\n```\n\n## Commit Message Body\n\nThe body answers: why was this change needed? What problem does it solve?\n\nDon't describe what the code does (the diff shows that). Write what a reviewer needs to understand the intent.\n\n## Voice\n\nUse active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\n\n## Scope Conventions (this repo)\n\n| Scope | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| `sentinel` | sentinel plugin and subagents |\n| `ranger` | ranger plugin and subagents |\n| `courier` | courier plugin and subagents |\n| `weaver` | weaver plugin and subagents |\n| `scribe` | scribe plugin and subagents |\n| `vanguard` | vanguard plugin and subagents |\n| `navigator` | navigator plugin and subagents |\n| `smith` | smith plugin and subagents |\n| `mason` | mason plugin and subagents |\n| `muse` | muse plugin and subagents |\n| `shared` | shared schemas, references, agent-best-practices |\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[86] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk gh pr close 95 --comment \\\"Closing as superseded by the release-recovery implementation. The approved workflow removes both the environment-policy check and environment: release, keeps production fail-closed pending rehearsal evidence, and makes the reviewed release-PR merge the sole human approval.\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Close PR #95 as the user authorized because it is superseded by the approved no-Environment recovery design?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"rtk\",\"gh\",\"pr\",\"close\"]}); text(r.output);\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[87] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 23.4 seconds\nOutput:\n\n✓ Closed pull request orin-dx/callisto#95 (chore(ci): remove the release environment's required-reviewer gate)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[88] assistant: PR #95 is now closed with a su