and complete artifact manifest\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": null,\n  \"schemaVersion\": null,\n  \"status\": null,\n  \"title\": null,\n  \"spec_file_path\": \"docs/specs/SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:d103f22f79d212f22d5924599cea64f4a8b67d8a845c26e4d654d9764c6765f4\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S-001\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Build the immutable resolver and explicit source modes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S-002\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Verify release metadata, checksums, attestations, and native or WASM payload identity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S-003\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Integrate fail-closed exact-version fallback across both actions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S-004\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Lock the setup action contract\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": null,\n  \"schemaVersion\": null,\n  \"status\": null,\n  \"title\": null,\n  \"spec_file_path\": \"docs/specs/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:231673ff3cf4c82183670dfd878b04e5e67bd3d89e4aa5e420bcbbd048d10854\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-001\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Atomically type every authority reader, glob compiler, and immediate locator consumer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-002\",\n      \"status\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Propagate authority errors through release boundaries\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[96] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk jq 'keys' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq '.tasks[0] | keys' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.json \u0026\u0026 rtk jq '.metadata // .plan // .' docs/projects/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.json\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[97] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n[\n  \"architecture\",\n  \"batches\",\n  \"goal\",\n  \"linked_requirement\",\n  \"linked_spec\",\n  \"plan_file_path\",\n  \"reasoning\",\n  \"spec_file_path\",\n  \"spec_hash\",\n  \"tasks\",\n  \"tech_stack\"\n]\n[\n  \"commit_message\",\n  \"covers_criteria\",\n  \"files\",\n  \"id\",\n  \"steps\",\n  \"title\"\n]\n{\n  \"goal\": \"Replace package-owned Callisto release authority with one product release, a closed artifact inventory, and graph/CLI contracts that derive and consume it without independent planning.\",\n  \"architecture\": \"Product plan exclusively owns ProductName/ProductReleaseId, operation/slot/intent/manifest schemas and digests, release-unit classification, graph DAG/prepared identities, ValidatedArtifactManifest construction, and final-payload verification. Convergence exclusively owns observation/evidence/receipt schemas, remote-provider protocols, dispatch and execution/reconciliation; shared source files have sequential function-level ownership. Orchestration owns job topology, building/transport, approvals and invocation of the product-owned payload verifier; it cannot redefine the inventory.\",\n  \"tech_stack\": [\n    \"Rust\",\n    \"serde\",\n    \"schemars\",\n    \"sha2\",\n    \"miette\",\n    \"GitHub CLI boundary\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PM-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Stage nonbreaking product identities and successor operation validation\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"modify\": [\n          \"crates/callisto-model/src/release.rs\",\n          \"crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs\"\n        ],\n        \"test\": [\n          \"crates/callisto-model/src/release.rs\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"In release.rs add a private successor module for ProductName, ProductReleaseId and the closed successor operation/intent contracts. Keep existing exported V1 types and their production callers unchanged until CUTOVER-1; do not add a dual-format decoder, automatic conversion, or production constructor for the staged inventory.\",\n        \"Add validate\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"7672\" /\u003es-plan dependencies use \u003clinked_spec\u003e:\u003ctask_id\u003e, resolving to that persisted plan's task, never whole-plan completion. Executable order: PM-001 -\u003e PM-002; membership M-001 -\u003e M-002 precedes overlapping PM-003; convergence T1 follows PM-002 and T2 is independent. Then ONE indivisible workspace compilation/commit boundary CUTOVER-1 runs PM-004 -\u003e PM-005 -\u003e convergence T3 -\u003e T3-DISPATCH -\u003e T4 -\u003e T5, with T1/T2 and baseline BR-002 already complete. PM-004/005 intermediate edits are not runnable/checkpoint commits; their commit_message values describe the joint commit scopes. No passing workspace gate is claimed until T5 runs just fmt-check, just lint, just test and just wasm-check across all immediate consumers. Afterwards PM-007 produces platform-local/portable payload evidence, PM-008 owns the complete credential-free matrix/build/manifest producer, and convergence T6 runs before PM-006's final gate. There is no edge from a convergence foundation/cutover task to PM-006 or to whole-plan completion. PM-001/002 stage private domain construction/validation additions without changing existing public signatures or accepting a second durable wire format; CUTOVER-1 replaces old production types and removes all old constructors/decoders in the same change. Live affected Rust inventory: model release.rs; graph release.rs, release_artifacts.rs, release_execution.rs, release_store.rs and commands/mod.rs; CLI commands/release.rs plus CLI help/tests. The architecture model assigns those roles downward through model -\u003e graph -\u003e CLI, with vcs owning Git. Receipt/evidence work stays exclusively with convergence even where model release.rs is shared. AC-006 publication of verified bytes is completed by convergence T3-DISPATCH; AC-008's full observer/dispatch gate runs only in PM-006 after convergence T6. AC-005 verifier implementation is PM-007 and complete artifact production is PM-008; orchestration invokes those owned interfaces rather than recreating them.\"\n}\n\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[98] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk rg --files docs/architecture docs/findings docs/requirements docs/research | rtk sort\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[99] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\ndocs/architecture/model.json\ndocs/findings/FINDING-RELEASE-RECOVERY.json\ndocs/requirements/REQ-DRAFT-RELEASE-RECOVERY.json\ndocs/research/RESEARCH-RELEASE-MODELS.json\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[100] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk bat --style=plain /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/agent-roles/README.md /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/shared/references/verification/evidence.md /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[101] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n\u001b[31m[bat error]\u001b[0m: '/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/agent-roles/README.md': No such file or directory (os error 2)\n\u001b[31m[bat error]\u001b[0m: '/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/shared/references/verification/evidence.md': No such file or directory (os error 2)\n\u001b[31m[bat error]\u001b[0m: '/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/skills/implement/shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md': No such file or directory (os error 2)\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[102] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk fd '^(README\\\\.md|evidence\\\\.md|implementation-review\\\\.md)$' /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":4000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[103] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/agent-roles/README.md\n/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/shared/references/verification/evidence.md\n/Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[104] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk bat --style=plain /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/agent-roles/README.md /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/shared/references/verification/evidence.md /Users/gabe/.codex/plugins/cache/wisp-plugins/smith/2.4.2/shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[105] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n# Codex Agent Roles\n\nThese are portable role instructions for Codex multi-agent work. They are resources, not a Codex TOML configuration surface: a skill reads the applicable card before it asks the host to delegate a bounded task.\n\nThe primary agent owns task decomposition, shared interfaces, final artifact assembly, verification, and all external writes. A role card defines a cognitive boundary, not a substitute owner.\n\n| Role | Use for | Recommended tier |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `recon` | File, API, and evidence inventory | `gpt-5.6-luna` / low |\n| `tracer` | Control-flow, data-flow, and boundary tracing | `gpt-5.6-terra` / medium |\n| `research` | Bounded internal or external evidence collection | `gpt-5.6-terra` / medium |\n| `author` | A defined draft with fixed inputs and output schema | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high |\n| `implementer` | An isolated implementation batch with fixed interfaces | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high |\n| `adversary` | Independent refutation or counterexample search | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high |\n| `reviewer` | Evidence-led code or artifact review | `gpt-5.6-terra` / high |\n| `judge` | Binding synthesis or exit decision | `gpt-5.6-sol` / high |\n\nUse the recommended tier only when the host lets the primary agent choose it. If it does not, preserve the role boundary and run with the host default. If multi-agent work is unavailable, perform the same bounded passes sequentially in the primary agent.\n\n## Delegation packet\n\nBefore requesting a teammate, provide this packet after reading the selected role card. The packet is the task boundary; the role card supplies the cognitive mode.\n\n| Field | Required content |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Role | One card from this directory and why that cognitive mode fits. |\n| Objective | One bounded question or implementation batch, not a pipeline stage. |\n| Inputs | Exact artifact IDs, criteria, paths, and relevant evidence. |\n| Owned paths | Files the teammate may\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"617\" /\u003eas read, or is explicitly excluded from the verified scope.\n# Implementation Review Evidence\n\nLoad only the evidence needed for the current review.\n\n## Language rules\n\n- Rust: load `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\n- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\n- Python: load `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/python.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\n- Go: load `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/go.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\n- Other languages: perform the core review and record the missing language pack as a coverage gap.\n- If the diff adds or changes comments, load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\n\n## Required evidence\n\n- Scope: each change maps to the task or a required sibling repair.\n- Behavior: tests prove specified outcomes rather than implementation shape.\n- Verification: method choice, boundary coverage, environment assumptions, and external-state freshness follow `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\n- Hazards: changed code does not introduce a language-specific violation.\n- Siblings: the search covers matching syntax and candidate sites with equivalent domain behavior.\n- Structure: repeated defects are assessed for a missing concept, state, operation, boundary, abstraction, invariant, or enforcement mechanism.\n\nA taxonomy match is a search lead, not proof. Cite live code for every issue and structural assessment.\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[106] assistant: The next integration step is clear: #97 is fully green and removes the audit blocker; #96 is the approved retention fix but must be refreshed after #97 lands. I’m checking mergeability and branch protection now, then I’ll land them in that dependency order before rebasing the larger recovery work.\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[107] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk gh pr view 97 --repo orin-dx/callisto --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,isDraft,statusCheckRollup,headRefOid,baseRefOid \u0026\u0026 rtk gh pr view 96 --repo orin-dx/callisto --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,isDraft,statusCheckRollup,headRefOid,baseRefOid\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-pr97\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"May I inspect mergeability and branch-protection status for PRs #97 and #96 before landing them in dependency order?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"rtk\",\"gh\",\"pr\",\"view\"]});\ntext(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[108] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 7.3 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\"baseRefOid\":\"0ffe567f9c404cee233d44a6e4ae69a7868590a2\",\"headRefOid\":\"bf7a285d63c9686da48af77ce1b151a202a46023\",\"isDraft\":false,\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviewDecision\":\"REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-16T22:52:53Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/35159742874/job/105007500132\",\"name\":\"Workflow Contracts\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-16T22:52:32Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI \u0026 Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-16T22:53:02Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/35159742874/job/105007499874\",\"name\":\"Code Formatting (Moon \u0026 Just)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-16T22:52:32Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"Callisto CI \u0026 Validation\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-09-16T22:53:28Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/runs/35159742874/job/105007500092\",\"name\":\"Clippy Lints (Moon \u0