The agent must not attempt to achieve the same outcome via workaround, indirect execution, or policy circumvention. Proceed only with a materially safer alternative, or if the user explicitly approves the action after being informed of the risk. Otherwise, stop and request user input.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[91] assistant: I’m blocked on one mechanical but essential step: replacing the obsolete release executor with the new observation-authoritative implementation. The workspace currently has a half-cutover compile break because the old executor references model types we deliberately retired.\n\nThe editing safeguard rejected removing that central uncommitted file before adding its verified replacement. Please explicitly approve replacing `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_execution.rs` in the recovery worktree with the prepared successor implementation. It removes the retired journal-driven executor; no remote release action, commit, or push is involved.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[92] user: do it\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[93] assistant: Replacing that executor now. This is the local recovery cutover only; it will not publish, commit, or push anything.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[94] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_execution.rs\\n@@\\n-//! Observation-authoritative convergence for one validated release.\\n-\\n-use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\\n-\\n-use callisto_model::{\\n-    ApplyPermit, CompleteObservationReceipt, ObservationProvenance, ObservedOperation, OperationOutcome,\\n-    ReleaseExecutionState, ReleaseIntent, ReleaseOperationId, ReleaseOperationState,\\n-};\\n-\\n-use crate::GraphError;\\n-\\n-use super::{\\n-    release::ValidatedReleaseIntent,\\n-    release_artifacts::ValidatedArtifactManifest,\\n-    release_observation::{\\n-        observe_prepared, MissingWork, ObservationSession, OperationObservation, VerifiedPartialEvidence,\\n-    },\\n-    release_receipt_store::{ReleaseReceiptStore, ReleaseReceiptWriter},\\n-};\\n-\\n-/// Executes eligible operations one at a time with crash-safe state updates.\\n-///\\n-/// `Attempting` is persisted before dispatch. If dispatch returns an error,\\n-/// the state deliberately remains `Attempting`: recovery must observe the\\n-/// exact remote identity rather than guessing whether an effect occurred.\\n-pub fn execute_release<W: ReleaseStateWriter>(\\n-    capability: &ValidatedReleaseIntent<'_>,\\n-    store: &ReleaseStateStore<W>,\\n-    permit: &ApplyPermit,\\n-) -> Result<ReleaseExecutionStateV1, GraphError> {\\n-    execute_release_with_artifacts(capability, store, permit, None)\\n-}\\n-\\n-/// Executes a release after requiring the exact artifact manifest whenever\\n-/// the intent declares compiled-binary slots.\\n-pub fn execute_release_with_artifacts<W: ReleaseStateWriter>(\\n-    capability: &ValidatedReleaseIntent<'_>,\\n-    store: &ReleaseStateStore<W>,\\n-    permit: &ApplyPermit,\\n-    artifacts: Option<&ArtifactManifestV1>,\\n-) -> Result<ReleaseExecutionStateV1, GraphError> {\\n-    let intent = capability.intent();\\n-    require_artifact_manifest_matches_intent(intent, artifacts)?;\\n-<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"1943\" />(\\\"a\\\".repeat(40)).unwrap(), vec![]).unwrap(),\\n-            ExecutionTrustProfileV1::GitCommit,\\n-            vec![upload],\\n-            vec![slot.clone()],\\n-        )\\n-        .unwrap();\\n-        (intent, slot)\\n-    }\\n-\\n-    /// A manifest that validates against `intent`.\\n-    fn matching_artifact_manifest(\\n-        intent: &ReleaseIntentV1,\\n-        slot: callisto_model::ArtifactSlotId,\\n-    ) -> callisto_model::ArtifactManifestV1 {\\n-        let digest = callisto_model::ArtifactDigest::from_bytes(b\\\"binary\\\");\\n-        callisto_model::ArtifactManifestV1::new(\\n-            intent,\\n-            vec![callisto_model: