lreadySatisfied).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(\n            reconcile_release_execution(&intent, &state).unwrap().eligible(),\n            &[forge]\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn non_successful_or_attempting_prerequisites_never_make_dependents_eligible() {\n        let intent = intent();\n        let publish = intent.operations[0].id().clone();\n        let tag = intent.operations[1].id().clone();\n        let mut state = ReleaseExecutionStateV1::pending(&intent);\n        state.mark_attempting(&publish).unwrap();\n        assert!(reconcile_release_execution(&intent, &state)\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[93] tool exec call: const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_execution.rs\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(typeof r === \"string\" ? r : JSON.stringify(r));\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[94] tool exec result: Script failed\nWall time 7.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\nScript error:\nThis action was rejected due to unacceptable risk.\nReason: Although the user approved replacing the executor, this standalone deletion is not an atomic replacement and would remove the current uncommitted file without a verified replacement in the same action.\nThe agent must not attempt to achieve the same outcome via workaround, indirect execution, or policy circumvention. Proceed only with a materially safer alternative, or if the user explicitly approves the action after being informed of the risk. Otherwise, stop and request user input.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[95] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk wc -l crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_execution.rs\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1000});\ntext(r.output);\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[96] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n118